  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The 2026 MotoGP season concluded with Ducati rider Marc Marquez officially clinching his eighth world championship title. This achievement followed his performance at the Portuguese Grand Prix, where an eighth-place finish secured enough points to confirm his season victory. With this result, Marquez has surpassed the championship record previously held by Valentino Rossi. Final standings for the season show Marquez leading with 439 points, followed by Jorge Martin with 396 points and Marco Bezzecchi with 394 points. Alongside the individual rider championship, Aprilia Racing successfully claimed the team world championship title for the 2026 season. Following the announcement, Marquez shared an emotional message dedicated to his supporters regarding the milestone. The conclusion of the season marks a significant shift in the sport's historical record books as the competition continues to evolve.",
